.TH MIOS\-VARIANTS 7 "" "MiOS 0.3.0" "MiOS Variants"
.SH NAME
mios\-variants \- the MiOS product line
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every variant below is one entry in the single source of truth.
The status is measured, not aspirational: shipping means
built, published and observed; partial means the machinery
runs but does not yet do the whole job; design means
specified with no artifact yet.
.SH VARIANTS
.TP
.B MiOS (shipping)
the base bootc host: the AI plane, the container plane and a Windows guest on one immutable image
.br
Runs on: bare metal or a virtual machine.
.TP
.B MiOS\-Cat (partial)
the portable edition: a Ventoy USB or NVMe carrying the image, the repository and the models to run, install and deploy with no network
.br
Runs on: removable USB or NVMe.
.TP
.B MiOS\-DEV (partial)
the development host: builds, bakes and gates the image, and runs MiOS itself as the container machine
.br
Runs on: a WSL2 machine on a workstation.
.TP
.B MiOS\-Metal (design)
the metal\-owning firmware: a small headless bootc hypervisor\-router that binds the GPUs and NICs and hosts MiOS as a guest
.br
Runs on: bare metal, headless.
.TP
.B MiOS\-Xbox (partial)
the gaming edition: an Xbox\-tuned Windows guest, gaming debloat posture and its own branding
.br
Runs on: bare metal or a virtual machine.
.TP
.B MiOS\-Xbox\-Arm (design)
the gaming edition for arm64 hardware, sharing the Xbox posture with an arm64 Windows guest
.br
Runs on: arm64 bare metal.
.SH NAMING
Titles read MiOS-<Suffix> and keys read mios-<suffix>: the same name in two registers.
A suffix names the job, not the size.
.SH SEE ALSO
